WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.226 --> 00:00:01.113
(audience applauding)
- So we have,

00:00:01.113 --> 00:00:04.610
someone on the line who is
very familiar with that song.

00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:07.035
Can we say hi to him, everybody?

00:00:07.035 --> 00:00:09.119
What's up Ed Sheeran.
(audience applauding)

00:00:09.119 --> 00:00:14.119
(upbeat music)
(audience applauding)

00:00:15.528 --> 00:00:18.003
Get it out. Get it out people.

00:00:18.003 --> 00:00:19.950
They love you.
(audience applauding)

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:21.580
It is great to see you again.

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:23.210
I will... I'm gonna lead with this.

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:24.930
It is absolutely terrifying

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:27.180
to be singing someone's
song and them listening

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:28.730
while you're doing it.
(laughing)

00:00:28.730 --> 00:00:30.460
I was like, "Oh my God!"

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:31.400
I was like, "It's Sheeran."

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:32.780
I love that song though.

00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:33.920
Bad habits is such a jam.

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:34.753
I love it.

00:00:34.753 --> 00:00:35.932
Why did you write that?

00:00:35.932 --> 00:00:36.765
- Thank you.

00:00:36.765 --> 00:00:37.810
I loved your version by the way.

00:00:37.810 --> 00:00:39.930
I was listening to your version,

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:41.550
wondering whether I
should have actually used

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:43.640
more electric guitar in
it cause it sounded...

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:45.120
Sounded pretty great.
(laughing)

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:47.399
I wrote here...

00:00:47.399 --> 00:00:49.343
One is by accident.

00:00:49.343 --> 00:00:51.550
I was working with

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:54.880
the two people that I'd
made the album with,

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:56.240
Johnny and Fred.

00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:59.150
And Fred is primarily
like a dance producer

00:00:59.150 --> 00:01:02.150
and he played me a tune that
he was just about to release.

00:01:02.150 --> 00:01:04.040
That was a really,
really heavy dance tune.

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:04.990
And I just said, you know what,

00:01:04.990 --> 00:01:07.569
let's just try and make something upbeat

00:01:07.569 --> 00:01:10.280
that could also be
played on acoustic guitar

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:11.590
and life basically.

00:01:11.590 --> 00:01:13.140
And yeah, it just kind
of happened by accident.

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:15.106
I wasn't expecting it to be first single

00:01:15.106 --> 00:01:17.900
and yeah it's one of these songs that

00:01:17.900 --> 00:01:20.400
it sort of came out and
it's just kind of stuck

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:21.542
and it's not like...

00:01:21.542 --> 00:01:26.280
It hasn't been like my
biggest charting single

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:27.779
but I think it'll end up being...

00:01:27.779 --> 00:01:28.612
- Longevity.

00:01:28.612 --> 00:01:29.970
- One of my biggest songs just over time.

00:01:29.970 --> 00:01:30.803
- Yeah. That's longevity.
- Very, very gradually.

00:01:30.803 --> 00:01:32.880
- And that's the best kind of song though.

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:35.200
And also I didn't wanna
freak you out but my idea was

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:37.280
actually to completely
do it with just a piano

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:39.380
and I wanted to make
it really dark and sad

00:01:39.380 --> 00:01:40.830
and then I didn't wanna freak you out.

00:01:40.830 --> 00:01:42.730
So I kept it like this one,
(laughing)

00:01:42.730 --> 00:01:44.100
but I love a song like that.

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:45.430
I feel like you write songs like that.

00:01:45.430 --> 00:01:47.610
That you can literally do with
a huge band electric guitars.

00:01:47.610 --> 00:01:48.830
Do it big. You could do dance.

00:01:48.830 --> 00:01:49.850
You could do singer, songwriter.

00:01:49.850 --> 00:01:51.940
I think it's an amazing gift you have.

00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:53.640
Songwriting. Everybody knows that.

